+# Local MAPF Negotiation Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Implement and measure an opt-in, bounded local joint planner for at most four RMF Traffic participants with safe fallback to existing negotiation.
+
+**Architecture:** A standalone `LocalConflictResolver` reuses each participant's RMF `Planner` in a bounded best-first search over priority orderings. `CentralizedNegotiation` calls it only when opted in and preserves its current table/rollout algorithm as fallback.
+
+**Tech Stack:** C++17, rmf_traffic Planner/schedule/conflict APIs, Catch2, CMake/colcon
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-03-local-mapf-negotiation-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Preserve baseline `ccdb765` and all holding-point alternative ranking behavior.
+- Modify only `rmf_traffic`; do not modify Fleet Adapter, `rmf_ros2`, external arbiters, or corridor managers/state machines.
+- Hard maximum of four agents; node, replan, and wall-time budgets are configurable.
+- No hardcoded map, corridor, waypoint, robot name, compass direction, or robot count.
+- Successful output is `std::unordered_map<schedule::ParticipantId, Plan>`; every local failure falls back to existing negotiation.
+- This is opt-in core feasibility, not a claimed production insertion point or complete MAPF implementation.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Local participant itineraries already in the schedule must be ignored without ignoring external traffic; Task 2 tests both.
+- Initial and terminal stationary occupancy must participate in conflict checks; Task 2 adds persistent-occupancy tests.
+- Synthetic reservations must not produce invalid schedule dependencies; Task 2 asserts returned plans contain no synthetic dependency.
+- Duplicate participant IDs, null planners, zero budgets, and more than four agents must fail deterministically; Task 1 tests validation.
+- Interruption or any budget exhaustion must preserve baseline fallback behavior; Task 3 tests each termination path.
+
+---
+
